##! # Binary DSL — Runtime support
##!
##! Runtime types for the `binary {}` block and `packed struct(uN)`
##! constructs locked in `docs/design/BINARY_DSL.md`.
##!
##! The compiler recognises these types; this module only holds the
##! user-visible enum + helpers. Real decode/encode logic lives in the
##! codegen pass (`cg_intrinsic_binary.qz`, sub-phase 1.4).
##!
##! @since 5.28.0

## Errors that a synthesised `.decode()` method may return.
##
## Design decision #5 (BINARY_DSL.md): errors-as-values. Every
## `binary {}` decode call returns `Result<T, ParseError>`. Panics
## never happen in the hot path — malformed inputs route through
## `match` like every other Result in the language.
enum ParseError
  ## Reached the end of the input before the layout demanded it.
  UnexpectedEof
  ## A validated field (e.g. a tagged-union discriminator) held a
  ## value the layout forbids. `field` is the field name, `expected`
  ## is a human-readable spec, `got` is what was observed.
  InvalidValue(field: String, expected: String, got: Int)
  ## A length-prefix declared a field longer than the remaining input.
  LengthOverflow(field: String, declared: Int, remaining: Int)
  ## Phase 2 Track B — discriminated-union decode read a value that no
  ## arm matched. Unit variant (tag=3) — the richer structured form of
  ## InvalidValue is preserved for user-validated fields.
  InvalidDiscriminant
end
